 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Agent form tools
+
+In browsers supporting declarative WebMCP, the sign-in page exposes `sign-in`
+and the sign-up page exposes `sign-up`. Both tools accept required `username`
+and `password` fields and use the same client-side submission flow as the UI.
+The browser presents the filled form for user submission before performing the
+account action (`toolautosubmit` is omitted). The agent receives the completion
+or error message after the API request finishes; credentials and tokens are
+never included in the tool response.
+
+Browsers without WebMCP support continue to use the forms normally.
+Run the submission tests with `node --test tests/form-tools.test.mjs` (Node 24+).
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
